1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,920
(Supported by KOCCA)

2
00:00:01,990 --> 00:00:03,289
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds are fictitious.)

3
00:00:03,290 --> 00:00:04,590
(Children were filmed under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:07,060
Where did you get this?

5
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:08,160
Give it back right now.

6
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:10,160
If you tell me how an unpublished book...

7
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:12,870
- ended up here. - Hurry up and give it to me.

8
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:15,200
Give it back. I said give it to me.

9
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:16,840
Hand it over right now.

10
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:31,980
I am sorry.

11
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:41,160
I apologize.

12
00:00:41,190 --> 00:00:43,330
It is a very important book to me, so I acted on instinct.

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,600
It is mine.

14
00:00:46,870 --> 00:00:50,270
Where did you get that? It is not even published yet.

15
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:53,740
Well, do I have to tell you that?

16
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:59,210
I saved you, and I ate a moth for you.

17
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:01,310
Is it really that hard to tell me one thing?

18
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:04,580
I do not know.

19
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:06,620
I just happened to get my hands on it.

20
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:07,790
I swear...

21
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,490
I mean, I...

22
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:15,290
I have been waiting for that book for a really long time.

23
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:16,530
Did something happen to the author?

24
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,400
I read volumes one and two over and over,

25
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:20,300
worrying if Byeol I and Moon Bear were doing well.

26
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:21,570
I have waited for years.

27
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,540
So please tell me.

28
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:31,710
Where did you get it?

29
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:37,020
I do not remember.

30
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:40,750
Seriously. Then can you lend it to me?

31
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:43,190
I will read it quickly and give it back.

32
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:45,890
No. I said no.

33
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:48,860
It is because I really need it right now.

34
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,030
Come in.

35
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:55,470
I am asking you so politely,

36
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:57,270
can you not at least pretend to listen?

37
00:01:59,010 --> 00:02:00,470
Are you okay?

38
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:02,440
Everyone is waiting outside.

39
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:09,320
(Ryu Min)

40
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:11,920
Min.

41
00:02:12,690 --> 00:02:13,919
Give her an autograph.

42
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:14,920
What?

43
00:02:15,390 --> 00:02:16,890
She says she is a fan.

44
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:19,660
We will talk about the book after filming.

45
00:02:20,230 --> 00:02:22,560
I have nothing more to say.

46
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:23,660
Hey, well...

47
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:26,430
(Ryu Min)

48
00:02:33,370 --> 00:02:34,840
Where should I...

49
00:02:34,970 --> 00:02:36,110
Excuse me?

50
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:37,810
My autograph.

51
00:02:41,010 --> 00:02:42,380
I told you not to come see me anymore.

52
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:43,980
I do not want you to see me like this.

53
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:47,990
I want that too.

54
00:02:48,090 --> 00:02:49,360
But...

55
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,760
what can I do when my feet keep bringing me here?

56
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:54,860
Cut, okay. Hey, the emotion was great.

57
00:02:54,890 --> 00:02:56,260
Let us shoot the reverse.

58
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:58,500
What is this, the moth effect or what?

59
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:00,530
How is everything getting an okay in one take?

60
00:03:00,770 --> 00:03:03,770
Hey, let us shoot this quickly without any bloopers, okay?

61
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:05,570
- Okay. - Okay.

62
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:08,210
- Hey. - Yes. Mouthwash?

63
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:13,410
- Producer. - Yes?

64
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:16,780
By any chance, is your friend already asleep?

65
00:03:17,850 --> 00:03:19,590
I am not sure.

66
00:03:19,690 --> 00:03:20,820
But...

67
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:23,490
before the female lead goes into the room,

68
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:26,090
he is supposed to come meet her.

69
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:28,390
Then shouldn't the lights be off?

70
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:33,100
- Right, yes. - Yes.

71
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:35,800
("Byeol I and Moon Bear")

72
00:03:46,510 --> 00:03:49,120
("Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 3)

73
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:00,060
Bear.

74
00:04:01,090 --> 00:04:04,030
Even though bamboo is so thin and tall,

75
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:06,770
the reason it does not break in a typhoon...

76
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:10,870
is because it is empty inside and has joints.

77
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:13,540
People have joints too,

78
00:04:13,610 --> 00:04:16,480
and when they despair, hurt,

79
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:20,910
part ways, and fail, they say one forms each time.

80
00:04:21,550 --> 00:04:22,550
(Nodding)

81
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,880
You are the same, right?

82
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:26,750
For the things people did wrong,

83
00:04:28,150 --> 00:04:30,220
I will apologize on their behalf.

84
00:04:31,790 --> 00:04:33,630
How could they do that?

85
00:04:34,890 --> 00:04:36,300
Just for their own greed,

86
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,730
how could they do that to their family?

87
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:45,710
Mom, why did you skip a meal again?

88
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:51,610
("Polyamory")

89
00:04:52,610 --> 00:04:53,680
What is this now?

90
00:04:55,650 --> 00:04:56,680
Your dad said...

91
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:00,890
I might understand him better if I read it.

92
00:05:06,190 --> 00:05:07,330
Where is he?

93
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:10,660
He should be in your room.

94
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,300
What are you doing? Get out.

95
00:05:20,370 --> 00:05:22,210
What is this?

96
00:05:22,270 --> 00:05:25,510
- I told you not to write about us. - Why not?

97
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:28,310
Why not? You said it yourself.

98
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:31,080
Everything a writer experiences is firewood.

99
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:33,120
You told me to burn it deep and keep burning it.

100
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:38,620
Do not melt your personal feelings into your writing.

101
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:40,160
Making money through writing is not easy.

102
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:42,660
I know it is hard to make money just by looking at you.

103
00:05:42,730 --> 00:05:46,100
Family, loyalty, love, duty, affection,

104
00:05:46,170 --> 00:05:47,930
pulling out things you do not feel to write about them,

105
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,170
you must have suffered so much.

106
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:51,600
(Gong Yu Il)

107
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,010
College.

108
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:55,740
You got into such a good one, so why go there?

109
00:05:55,810 --> 00:05:57,180
They offered me a scholarship.

110
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,580
Hey, if it is about money, I will...

111
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:00,380
I do not need it anymore.

112
00:06:00,450 --> 00:06:03,420
Because I will not accept any help from you.

113
00:06:14,190 --> 00:06:15,530
Cut, okay.

114
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:17,660
Great work, everyone.

115
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:19,970
- Great work. - Great work, Director.

116
00:06:20,030 --> 00:06:21,770
- Great work. - Great work.

117
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:24,170
Yes, head back. Good job.

118
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:27,270
Did she fall asleep already?

119
00:06:28,370 --> 00:06:29,410
Whatever.

120
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,340
Does she think I cannot find it without her?

121
00:06:31,410 --> 00:06:33,950
I do not think you can find it. You have not found it for years,

122
00:06:34,010 --> 00:06:35,450
so how will you find it now?

123
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:37,920
Instead of hitting me with facts,

124
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:41,320
- give me some hope or something. - But...

125
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:43,520
My mouth feels dry, so how about a glass of beer?

126
00:06:43,590 --> 00:06:44,860
Forget it.

127
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,490
I knew I'd get rejected.

128
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,830
I'll let it slide since you're handsome.

129
00:06:48,990 --> 00:06:53,000
Oh, my, who is this? I'm finally seeing you.

130
00:06:53,070 --> 00:06:55,470
My daughter told me you were filming a movie here.

131
00:06:55,530 --> 00:06:58,940
- Oh, my, I wondered if it was true. - Yes, it's true.

132
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,240
Could I get a handshake?

133
00:07:02,310 --> 00:07:03,310
Sure.

134
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,880
I'll definitely watch the live broadcast.

135
00:07:06,950 --> 00:07:10,150
- I'll go see the movie too. - Yes, thank you.

136
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:12,990
- Let me take a picture too. - Ma'am, about the picture...

137
00:07:13,050 --> 00:07:14,190
No, it's fine.

138
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:18,390
- How long have you been waiting? - Oh, not that long.

139
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:20,230
I only waited three hours.

140
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:22,500
I thought my knees were going to kill me.

141
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,600
But seeing your face cures it all.

142
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:29,170
- Oh, thank you. Good luck. - Yes.

143
00:07:29,270 --> 00:07:30,700
- Yes. - Yes, I'll be going.

144
00:07:30,770 --> 00:07:32,340
- Yes. - Good luck.

145
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:37,680
We're packing up.

146
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:39,880
We're packing up.

147
00:07:41,610 --> 00:07:43,950
Mu I, earlier, when you were saving that woman,

148
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:47,420
you almost got seriously hurt. Don't do that from now on.

149
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:49,020
Okay.

150
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:51,959
- Yeong Su. - Yes.

151
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,790
It's a huge relief I didn't get hurt, right?

152
00:07:54,230 --> 00:07:56,130
Do you even have to ask?

153
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,230
You have movie stage greetings and a bunch of shoots lined up.

154
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:00,830
That's what I'm saying.

155
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,640
I'm that busy.

156
00:08:05,810 --> 00:08:07,040
So about that,

157
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:09,440
you need to do something for me.

158
00:08:09,510 --> 00:08:11,110
What? Do what?

159
00:08:18,250 --> 00:08:20,090
I thought you didn't have a shoot.

160
00:08:20,150 --> 00:08:23,420
- What brings you here? - It's about that incident.

161
00:08:24,590 --> 00:08:27,730
Tak Mu I said he would just let that go.

162
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:31,130
He was going to let it go. But thinking about it,

163
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:33,430
he thought you must have been very shocked that day, Gong Yu Il,

164
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:37,700
so Mu I was worried and sent this.

165
00:08:37,770 --> 00:08:39,310
What?

166
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,310
He's not the type to do that.

167
00:08:44,010 --> 00:08:45,210
Our Mu I,

168
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:47,050
sometimes when he gets fixated on something, he only sees that,

169
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,920
so he can be a little late to notice his surroundings.

170
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:54,920
I think you're similar in that regard.

171
00:08:58,920 --> 00:08:59,930
The stalker fan.

172
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,960
I'm sorry about that.

173
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:12,240
My mistake. Well, since I'm already apologizing,

174
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:16,310
let me apologize for one more thing. By any chance,

175
00:09:16,410 --> 00:09:19,010
could you lend me Volume Three of "Byeol I and Moon Bear"?

176
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,210
I knew it.

177
00:09:21,510 --> 00:09:22,850
Ta-da.

178
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:24,250
(The next day)

179
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:26,290
I wondered if you might have changed your mind overnight,

180
00:09:26,350 --> 00:09:27,420
so I came back.

181
00:09:27,490 --> 00:09:29,920
Could you lend "Byeol I and Moon Bear"...

182
00:09:29,990 --> 00:09:31,190
I'm sorry.

183
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:36,000
(The day after that)

184
00:09:36,060 --> 00:09:40,330
I brought some premium beef, so "Byeol I and Moon Bear"...

185
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:44,240
Well, if you don't want to lend it,

186
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:46,310
he told me to ask if you're willing to sell it, so I...

187
00:09:46,370 --> 00:09:50,340
- Oh my. - I said no, I'm not selling it.

188
00:09:50,410 --> 00:09:52,540
Do I have to sell everything just because he tells me to?

189
00:09:52,610 --> 00:09:55,780
I wouldn't sell it even if Tak Mu I's grandfather came.

190
00:09:55,850 --> 00:09:58,520
- Absolutely never. - Oh, my.

191
00:09:58,580 --> 00:09:59,590
Well...

192
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,100
It melts in my mouth, probably because it's premium beef.

193
00:10:19,810 --> 00:10:21,440
Does she really hate me?

194
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:24,410
I am Tak Mu I, after all.

195
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:26,950
That is the problem. It is because you are Tak Mu I.

196
00:10:27,010 --> 00:10:29,480
You treated an innocent person like a stalker,

197
00:10:29,550 --> 00:10:30,920
so I would not give it to you either.

198
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:34,120
You were worse than me!

199
00:10:35,490 --> 00:10:38,160
That is because my actor said she was a stalker,

200
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:41,260
so without a single doubt, I accused her.

201
00:10:41,330 --> 00:10:43,930
Exactly, so I am dying here.

202
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,630
Without a single moment of hesitation,

203
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:48,100
should we go just one more time?

204
00:10:48,170 --> 00:10:50,840
If you go one more time,

205
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,640
I think I will be reported as a stalker.

206
00:10:53,710 --> 00:10:54,970
She even said that even if your grandfather came,

207
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:57,010
she would absolutely never sell it.

208
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,880
Then do you want to go with my grandmother?

209
00:11:00,110 --> 00:11:02,250
No, let us send Min.

210
00:11:02,310 --> 00:11:04,120
She might give up the book since she is a fan of Min.

211
00:11:05,250 --> 00:11:06,250
Open wide.

212
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:09,250
You can eat at a time like this?

213
00:11:13,190 --> 00:11:14,290
It goes down just fine.

214
00:11:16,330 --> 00:11:17,800
Are you not going to eat?

215
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:21,530
Hey. We are getting too close these days.

216
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:22,600
When I moved in here,

217
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:24,140
you only visited once and never came back,

218
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:27,370
but now, you are coming over way too often.

219
00:11:32,510 --> 00:11:33,550
An autograph.

220
00:11:35,950 --> 00:11:37,780
- Ta-da. - Hey.

221
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:41,620
What is this? Why are you giving this to me now?

222
00:11:46,930 --> 00:11:48,090
What are you doing?

223
00:11:48,630 --> 00:11:50,860
If I die like this, engrave it on my tombstone.

224
00:11:50,930 --> 00:11:52,660
"Died from being too touched."

225
00:11:54,570 --> 00:11:56,570
("I Didn't Know Back Then")

226
00:11:57,570 --> 00:11:59,270
Hey, what is this?

227
00:12:00,570 --> 00:12:02,010
Ta-da.

228
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:04,880
- Are you a flower? - Yes.

229
00:12:05,010 --> 00:12:06,580
Gosh, how childish.

230
00:12:06,650 --> 00:12:09,950
- Are you not busy? - You were worried, so I wondered.

231
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:11,250
I was too curious to hold back.

232
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:12,620
(Da Hong came instead of flowers.)

233
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,920
I even missed the VIP premiere because of the shoot.

234
00:12:16,390 --> 00:12:17,420
Hey,

235
00:12:17,490 --> 00:12:19,730
you are putting in way too much unnecessary effort.

236
00:12:22,290 --> 00:12:27,100
This is my passionate devotion for you.

237
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:28,800
Tteokbokki. Oh, my.

238
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:33,540
I just ate earlier.

239
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:35,670
Are you eating again after you already had a meal?

240
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,880
I have to.

241
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:41,180
It is delicious.

242
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:44,120
You are so lucky.

243
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:46,290
You do not gain weight even when you eat that much.

244
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,250
- Eat some. - I am good.

245
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,160
He sleeps so well even with us talking.

246
00:12:52,790 --> 00:12:55,490
- Did he not sleep yesterday either? - He could not sleep all night,

247
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:58,130
and it seems he fell asleep for a bit at dawn,

248
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:00,200
so I practically had to carry him out to get here.

249
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,400
I feel so bad for him.

250
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,110
- What is that? - It is a bear.

251
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:14,780
- It is a bear. - It is a bear.

252
00:13:14,850 --> 00:13:16,980
- It is a bear. - Oh, no, it is a bear.

253
00:13:17,050 --> 00:13:18,850
- Hold on a second. - Stay back. It is dangerous.

254
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,920
- What do we do? - A bear came down.

255
00:13:20,990 --> 00:13:23,820
- What? There is a bear in front. - We are trapped.

256
00:13:23,890 --> 00:13:26,460
- It is coming. - Shoot it quickly.

257
00:13:26,530 --> 00:13:28,490
Shoot it quickly. It is running away!

258
00:13:45,310 --> 00:13:46,980
Mu I.

259
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,080
Mu I.

260
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:54,950
What is it? Did you have a dream?

261
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,260
What?

262
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:01,930
- Yes. - What dream makes you sweat?

263
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,230
When interpreting dreams, Ju Da Hong is the best.

264
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:07,930
Tell me. I will see if it is a dream about the movie becoming a huge hit.

265
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:09,570
Yes.

266
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:10,640
Well...

267
00:14:13,010 --> 00:14:14,170
Moon Bear...

268
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,740
No.

269
00:14:15,810 --> 00:14:17,740
- A moon bear... - Yes.

270
00:14:17,810 --> 00:14:19,580
It came down to the village to find food.

271
00:14:21,210 --> 00:14:23,680
Then it got shot,

272
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:24,980
and blood...

273
00:14:25,050 --> 00:14:28,490
The half-moon shape on its chest turned red.

274
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:34,030
And then,

275
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:35,990
it started losing consciousness.

276
00:14:37,230 --> 00:14:38,760
- Losing consciousness? - Losing consciousness?

277
00:14:40,870 --> 00:14:41,870
But,

278
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,970
that was me.

279
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:48,210
What?

280
00:14:48,270 --> 00:14:50,280
So it was not just a nonsense dream, it was a bear dream?

281
00:14:53,650 --> 00:14:54,650
I get it.

282
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:57,820
You said the Moon Bear was hungry.

283
00:14:59,890 --> 00:15:01,390
Mu I, you are hungry right now too, right?

284
00:15:01,450 --> 00:15:03,120
That is it.

285
00:15:03,190 --> 00:15:04,359
- Eat up. - That's right.

286
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:07,130
A well-fed bear has a shiny coat. Here.

287
00:15:07,190 --> 00:15:08,730
- I am fine. - Just one bite.

288
00:15:08,790 --> 00:15:10,200
- I am not eating. - Just take one bite.

289
00:15:10,260 --> 00:15:11,460
- I said I am not eating! - Just one bite.

290
00:15:12,830 --> 00:15:13,830
Hey.

291
00:15:15,470 --> 00:15:17,140
- Oh, seriously. - Hey.

292
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,200
Sorry.

293
00:15:20,410 --> 00:15:22,810
- Enjoy the movie. - I am a big fan.

294
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:25,880
Hello.

295
00:15:27,450 --> 00:15:31,020
Oh, why did I have to cover a shift on a day like this?

296
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:33,150
At this point, even I would not believe it.

297
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,820
("I Didn't Know Back Then" Premiere)

298
00:15:36,890 --> 00:15:40,360
(Theater 1 Exit)

299
00:15:41,990 --> 00:15:44,600
He will definitely think I followed him again.

300
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:47,670
("I Didn't Know Back Then" Premiere)

301
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,710
The actors will now enter.

302
00:15:58,510 --> 00:16:00,510
("I Didn't Know Back Then" Premiere)

303
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:05,020
Go, Tak Mu I!

304
00:16:06,990 --> 00:16:08,090
You are so handsome.

305
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:11,290
Let's hit ten million.

306
00:16:12,820 --> 00:16:13,960
Go for it.

307
00:16:15,590 --> 00:16:16,830
Go for it.

308
00:16:19,430 --> 00:16:20,500
("I Didn't Know Back Then," reach ten million viewers!)

309
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,100
- Why are you acting like this? - Get out.

310
00:16:25,170 --> 00:16:26,470
It is a bear.

311
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:29,710
- Do not move. - A bear is here.

312
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,140
A bear.

313
00:16:31,210 --> 00:16:32,780
We have to kill the bear!

314
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:40,720
- We have to kill the bear. - Catch it.

315
00:16:40,790 --> 00:16:43,060
Hey, what is wrong with you? Are you okay?

316
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:44,690
- Hey, Mu I. - What is it?

317
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:46,390
He is leaving.

318
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:50,130
- What is it? - Hey, why are you... Hey, Mu I.

319
00:16:54,830 --> 00:16:57,970
Hey, Mu I. What is wrong with you?

320
00:16:59,740 --> 00:17:00,870
What should we do about this?

321
00:17:01,910 --> 00:17:04,440
Excuse me, ma'am. Close the door, quickly.

322
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,910
- Excuse me, do you have a bag? - What? A bag?

323
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:09,050
A bag.

324
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:14,150
I am sorry.

325
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:17,560
Hey, Mu I, try to breathe.

326
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:20,590
Please try to breathe, please. A bag.

327
00:17:20,990 --> 00:17:22,360
A bag, quickly.

328
00:17:25,630 --> 00:17:26,800
Breathe.

329
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:33,040
Are you okay?

330
00:17:52,390 --> 00:17:53,390
Da Hong.

331
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:55,790
Mu I, are you awake?

332
00:17:55,860 --> 00:17:57,860
(Gangseong General Hospital)

333
00:17:57,930 --> 00:17:59,200
We are at Jae Gyu's hospital.

334
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:01,300
Yeong Su went back to the office for a bit.

335
00:18:01,370 --> 00:18:03,700
They said you suddenly started hyperventilating.

336
00:18:03,770 --> 00:18:04,770
Do you remember?

337
00:18:06,670 --> 00:18:08,209
What time is it? What about the premiere?

338
00:18:08,210 --> 00:18:10,240
Stay lying down.

339
00:18:10,310 --> 00:18:11,880
It is already over.

340
00:18:12,980 --> 00:18:14,150
It must've been a disaster.

341
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:16,650
Do you want me to show you?

342
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:18,450
For your peace of mind,

343
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:19,920
it would be best if you did not look at it.

344
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:25,120
Never mind. I will just read them to you.

345
00:18:25,190 --> 00:18:27,490
Mild or spicy?

346
00:18:27,590 --> 00:18:30,260
I will take the mild version, please.

347
00:18:30,730 --> 00:18:31,730
Okay.

348
00:18:32,830 --> 00:18:35,300
(Tak Mu I Premiere)

349
00:18:35,370 --> 00:18:37,570
"I even took a day off to see Tak Mu I,"

350
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,140
"but at the public premiere,"

351
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,870
"he barely showed his face before leaving."

352
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:42,310
"Tak Mu I from 'I Didn't Know Back Then.'"

353
00:18:42,370 --> 00:18:43,940
"I did not know he would be like this."

354
00:18:44,010 --> 00:18:45,510
"Power trip by the lead actor?"

355
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:47,910
"Does Tak Mu I look down on moviegoers?"

356
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:48,980
"Tak Mu I's blockbuster,"

357
00:18:49,050 --> 00:18:50,650
"audience anticipation ratings plummet."

358
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:51,950
"To blame it on a no-show..."

359
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:53,490
(Gangseong General Hospital)

360
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:55,220
Wait,

361
00:18:55,290 --> 00:18:58,460
excuse me, ma'am. I ordered the mild version.

362
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:01,360
This is the mild version.

363
00:19:01,430 --> 00:19:04,430
Do you want me to serve up the spicy one instead?

364
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:08,430
Da Hong, sometimes you are truly too cruel.

365
00:19:11,570 --> 00:19:12,570
Yes?

366
00:19:13,710 --> 00:19:14,870
Are you feeling better?

367
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:19,310
- Yes. - This was delivered for you.

368
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,950
Who sent it?

369
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:27,650
A courier dropped it off a little while ago.

370
00:19:30,790 --> 00:19:32,020
That I was admitted...

371
00:19:32,090 --> 00:19:33,460
No.

372
00:19:33,530 --> 00:19:36,260
Is it known that I am at this hospital?

373
00:19:36,330 --> 00:19:39,600
No, Dr. Jae Gyu told us to keep it a secret.

374
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:42,600
But the courier seemed to know everything when he arrived.

375
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,570
(Why did that happen?)

376
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,910
(Are you okay? I'm so worried.)

377
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:52,940
Where are you going?

378
00:20:12,330 --> 00:20:14,130
Excuse me, sir!

379
00:20:16,970 --> 00:20:18,270
Sir!

380
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:20,040
- Are you okay? - Oh, my.

381
00:20:20,410 --> 00:20:22,070
Her phone number?

382
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:23,980
I have no idea.

383
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:26,040
I was just coming out from another delivery,

384
00:20:26,110 --> 00:20:28,210
and some woman asked if I was a courier.

385
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:31,420
I said yes, I am, and asked if it was not obvious.

386
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,750
Then she just shoved 50 dollars into my hand...

387
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:36,190
and handed me that blue paper bag.

388
00:20:36,250 --> 00:20:39,320
For such a short distance, she didn't even ask about the fee...

389
00:20:39,390 --> 00:20:40,990
and just gave me 50 dollars,

390
00:20:41,060 --> 00:20:43,360
so I did think it was a little strange.

391
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:45,700
By any chance, did that woman...

392
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:47,630
have short hair,

393
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,870
a petite build, and pale skin?

394
00:20:49,940 --> 00:20:52,870
What? She was quite tall.

395
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:54,840
And I think her hair was really long.

396
00:20:54,910 --> 00:20:56,910
Her skin was on the tanner side too.

397
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:59,410
Anyway, she was sexy.

398
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:02,580
She was dripping with sex appeal from head to toe.

399
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:06,850
Hey, you are not even feeling well.

400
00:21:08,150 --> 00:21:09,390
Are you okay?

401
00:21:09,450 --> 00:21:12,220
What happened? Did you catch them? Who did he say sent it?

402
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:19,730
I already have a million things to worry about.

403
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:24,570
- Darn it, seriously. - Why? Are you okay?

404
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:26,000
- What is it? - Are you okay?

405
00:21:27,410 --> 00:21:29,470
(Why did that happen?)

406
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:31,110
(Are you okay? I'm so worried.)

407
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:53,730
Why aren't you answering your phone?

408
00:21:55,330 --> 00:21:58,870
- Grandma! - Oh, come here. Oh, my baby.

409
00:21:58,940 --> 00:22:00,670
Grandma.

410
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:05,010
- What brings you here so early? - I was on my way to a shoot nearby.

411
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:07,310
- I see. - Get up, you need to eat something.

412
00:22:08,310 --> 00:22:09,550
I'm fine.

413
00:22:10,080 --> 00:22:12,920
I've been getting so much hate lately,

414
00:22:12,980 --> 00:22:14,520
I feel like I'm going to burst.

415
00:22:14,590 --> 00:22:16,520
I heard you're starting a new project right away.

416
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:17,920
Good for you.

417
00:22:17,990 --> 00:22:19,320
It's better to stay busy at times like this.

418
00:22:20,490 --> 00:22:21,990
I think so too.

419
00:22:22,690 --> 00:22:25,600
Work on your project, and date too.

420
00:22:25,660 --> 00:22:26,930
Are you seeing anyone?

421
00:22:28,300 --> 00:22:29,300
No.

422
00:22:30,570 --> 00:22:32,600
Don't forget your promise to me.

423
00:22:32,870 --> 00:22:34,870
The condition for you to keep acting.

424
00:22:34,940 --> 00:22:36,710
Whether it's marriage or dating,

425
00:22:36,780 --> 00:22:38,680
you only do it with someone in the same industry.

426
00:22:40,050 --> 00:22:41,080
Not this again.

427
00:22:42,380 --> 00:22:43,580
Mu I.

428
00:22:45,350 --> 00:22:48,390
- Ma'am! - How have you been?

429
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:52,190
Yes. You haven't changed a bit.

430
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,390
Oh, you've gotten even prettier.

431
00:22:55,490 --> 00:22:56,830
Mu I.

432
00:22:56,900 --> 00:22:58,530
If you're going to date anyone, date Da Hong.

433
00:22:59,730 --> 00:23:02,000
Why would I date her?

434
00:23:02,070 --> 00:23:04,200
Why not? She's bright and lovely.

435
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:07,740
Since you do the same work, you'll understand each other well.

436
00:23:07,810 --> 00:23:09,310
Right, Ma'am?

437
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:11,640
What now?

438
00:23:11,710 --> 00:23:13,080
How did you get in?

439
00:23:13,650 --> 00:23:15,080
I ran into Yeong Su out front.

440
00:23:15,150 --> 00:23:17,420
- Oh, you're here? - Yes.

441
00:23:17,820 --> 00:23:20,450
Da Hong said she was going to eat with Mu I...

442
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:21,950
and go to the commercial shoot together,

443
00:23:22,020 --> 00:23:23,620
so she told me to open the door.

444
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:25,160
And you just let her in?

445
00:23:25,220 --> 00:23:26,790
Who can say no to Da Hong?

446
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:28,830
- Oh, man. - Good job.

447
00:23:28,890 --> 00:23:30,560
Don't say no to her in the future, either.

448
00:23:30,630 --> 00:23:32,530
Never say no to her.

449
00:23:32,600 --> 00:23:33,730
You're the best, ma'am.

450
00:23:35,170 --> 00:23:36,600
I brought sushi. Let's eat together.

451
00:23:36,670 --> 00:23:37,770
Oh, let's do that.

452
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,210
I'll go plate it.

453
00:23:40,270 --> 00:23:42,770
Because an actress has to eat beautifully, even for one bite.

454
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:43,840
Right.

455
00:23:47,710 --> 00:23:50,620
She's bright and lovely. She's so pretty.

456
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:51,950
I told you, no.

457
00:23:54,650 --> 00:23:56,490
Other older people usually don't like celebrities,

458
00:23:56,550 --> 00:23:59,160
but she seems a bit unique, right?

459
00:23:59,260 --> 00:24:01,730
You didn't know? Her husband.

460
00:24:01,790 --> 00:24:02,790
What?

461
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:08,930
I mean, Mu I's grandfather was a very ordinary guy.

462
00:24:09,030 --> 00:24:12,970
He worked at some small company. But after marrying her,

463
00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:14,840
with all her scandals and rumors,

464
00:24:14,910 --> 00:24:17,040
and her being away for days on out-of-town shoots,

465
00:24:17,110 --> 00:24:20,150
he suffered from severe depression...

466
00:24:20,210 --> 00:24:21,350
and took his own...

467
00:24:22,350 --> 00:24:23,580
Really?

468
00:24:24,050 --> 00:24:25,520
Keep your voice down.

469
00:24:25,580 --> 00:24:26,580
Just plate the food.

470
00:24:26,790 --> 00:24:28,520
("Tak Mu I Trashes Conscience, Is He a Controversy Maker?")

471
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:38,160
You remember, right?

472
00:24:38,660 --> 00:24:40,130
How Volume Two ended.

473
00:24:41,370 --> 00:24:42,430
Because of the bear bile extraction,

474
00:24:42,500 --> 00:24:45,100
the mother bear who suffered her whole life in a cage died,

475
00:24:48,640 --> 00:24:49,870
Yes.

476
00:24:49,940 --> 00:24:51,440
And Moon Bear, who was rescued alone,

477
00:24:51,510 --> 00:24:54,080
grew up healthy with the love of the zoo family,

478
00:24:54,150 --> 00:24:55,910
and the night before returning to the wild,

479
00:24:55,980 --> 00:24:57,980
it ends right there.

480
00:24:58,050 --> 00:24:59,120
I think it did.

481
00:25:00,550 --> 00:25:01,820
So,

482
00:25:02,590 --> 00:25:05,360
I need to see it with my own eyes that the released Moon Bear...

483
00:25:05,420 --> 00:25:09,260
is doing well for this long nightmare to end.

484
00:25:10,500 --> 00:25:11,500
So, then...

485
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:14,030
do we go to that rooftop woman and take it by force?

486
00:25:14,130 --> 00:25:16,200
Or should we steal it?

487
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:17,540
Are we robbers?

488
00:25:19,740 --> 00:25:22,540
The publisher. Let us go to the publisher.

489
00:25:22,610 --> 00:25:24,279
- Hi. - Oh, you are here?

490
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:26,010
- Yes, hi. - Min Ye.

491
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:27,610
Your waiting room is over there.

492
00:25:29,710 --> 00:25:31,580
I thought your waiting room was the same as mine.

493
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:34,450
It has been a while, Mu I.

494
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:36,150
Yes, have you been well?

495
00:25:36,220 --> 00:25:38,290
Of course I have.

496
00:25:38,360 --> 00:25:42,830
But it seems like you have not been doing so well lately.

497
00:25:42,890 --> 00:25:46,500
This advertiser is something else. It should have just been you and me.

498
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:47,970
Why did they have to include her?

499
00:25:48,030 --> 00:25:51,570
The concept is "I will never yield." Not the man, not the coffee.

500
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:54,440
Why did you do that with the lunchbox?

501
00:25:54,510 --> 00:25:56,640
If you were to throw it away, should have done it out of sight.

502
00:25:57,280 --> 00:25:58,880
And as for the movie...

503
00:25:59,710 --> 00:26:00,710
How is it doing?

504
00:26:02,580 --> 00:26:03,650
Never mind.

505
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:06,250
Come to think of it, there are actors who work for movies...

506
00:26:06,320 --> 00:26:07,920
and actors who work for TV.

507
00:26:09,050 --> 00:26:12,090
Right. And you seem to work for YouTube.

508
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:15,830
- What? - The drama you finished recently...

509
00:26:15,890 --> 00:26:17,360
did not get a single article written about it,

510
00:26:17,430 --> 00:26:19,630
but your vlog is making a huge fuss.

511
00:26:21,130 --> 00:26:22,300
It is so strange.

512
00:26:22,370 --> 00:26:24,540
Usually, if people are curious about what someone eats, wears,

513
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:26,700
carries, or puts on,

514
00:26:26,770 --> 00:26:28,910
they are also curious about their actual job.

515
00:26:30,070 --> 00:26:31,380
Hey.

516
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:33,610
At least I am starting a new project right away.

517
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:36,450
Right, and for that project,

518
00:26:36,510 --> 00:26:39,780
- thank me for getting it. - Why would I?

519
00:26:39,850 --> 00:26:41,490
I turned that one down.

520
00:26:41,950 --> 00:26:44,260
If you want to keep picking up my leftovers,

521
00:26:46,690 --> 00:26:49,130
You should show some deep gratitude...

522
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:52,200
in a not-so-boring way.

523
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:55,530
You...

524
00:26:55,600 --> 00:26:57,700
I am going to check, and if you are lying, you are dead.

525
00:26:57,770 --> 00:26:58,770
Okay.

526
00:27:01,510 --> 00:27:03,040
Goodbye.

527
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:06,380
Ju Da Hong wins by knockout.

528
00:27:07,650 --> 00:27:09,280
You are very reliable.

529
00:27:09,710 --> 00:27:11,580
If someone scratches my guy, I claw them.

530
00:27:14,050 --> 00:27:15,090
Meow.

531
00:27:17,490 --> 00:27:18,520
I am sorry.

532
00:27:18,590 --> 00:27:21,530
All the senior staff happen to be on a business trip overseas.

533
00:27:21,590 --> 00:27:24,530
It is fine. Did you find anything out?

534
00:27:24,560 --> 00:27:27,430
Right. The book was not officially published.

535
00:27:27,500 --> 00:27:30,070
They only printed a few copies as proofreading drafts.

536
00:27:30,130 --> 00:27:33,500
Like the paper, illustrations, and things like that as a draft.

537
00:27:34,170 --> 00:27:36,410
Even then, only a few people involved...

538
00:27:36,470 --> 00:27:38,310
and the author received copies.

539
00:27:40,310 --> 00:27:42,010
Would the publisher not have one?

540
00:27:42,080 --> 00:27:43,080
No.

541
00:27:43,150 --> 00:27:45,150
I looked for it, but we do not have it.

542
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:47,690
When our publishing company moved,

543
00:27:47,820 --> 00:27:49,790
we probably threw them away.

544
00:27:59,460 --> 00:28:02,130
How on earth does Gong Yu Il have a book like that?

545
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:04,770
Was she affiliated with the publisher?

546
00:28:04,840 --> 00:28:07,170
No, she is too young for that.

547
00:28:07,240 --> 00:28:08,710
Mr. Tak.

548
00:28:08,770 --> 00:28:09,770
- Yes. - The scene...

549
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:12,080
we shot here last time, where you were eating ice cream...

550
00:28:12,140 --> 00:28:13,910
They said you have to reshoot it.

551
00:28:13,980 --> 00:28:16,880
- Why? - Min's acting was lacking,

552
00:28:16,950 --> 00:28:18,620
so his agency wants to reshoot it.

553
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:21,190
- I see. - I am sorry. It is because of me.

554
00:28:21,250 --> 00:28:22,590
No, it is fine.

555
00:28:23,690 --> 00:28:25,190
- Si Eun. My clothes from yesterday. - Yes.

556
00:28:25,260 --> 00:28:26,260
Oh, okay.

557
00:28:28,460 --> 00:28:29,730
It is fine.

558
00:28:33,260 --> 00:28:34,870
You don't have the clothes?

559
00:28:34,930 --> 00:28:37,100
I clearly told them that we might have to reshoot...

560
00:28:37,170 --> 00:28:38,740
and to keep them ready.

561
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:42,740
Oh, that shirt just disappeared without a trace.

562
00:28:43,140 --> 00:28:45,210
Gosh, what should we do?

563
00:28:45,280 --> 00:28:48,350
It is a continuity issue, so we cannot even change the outfit.

564
00:28:48,410 --> 00:28:51,820
Min's CEO begged me so much.

565
00:28:51,880 --> 00:28:55,020
And Min said he practiced his acting all night.

566
00:28:56,890 --> 00:28:58,760
Could we reshoot it tomorrow?

567
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:00,290
I will try to find something similar.

568
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:02,390
Well, it cannot be helped.

569
00:29:02,490 --> 00:29:06,100
I will explain it well to the director.

570
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:07,930
- I am sorry. - It is fine.

571
00:29:09,530 --> 00:29:10,540
I am sorry!

572
00:29:12,540 --> 00:29:13,540
It is fine.

573
00:29:22,910 --> 00:29:23,920
Are you not leaving?

574
00:29:25,850 --> 00:29:27,020
I am going to sleep here tonight.

575
00:29:29,490 --> 00:29:31,160
Since you helped me with the script reading,

576
00:29:31,220 --> 00:29:32,620
I should repay you.

577
00:29:32,660 --> 00:29:35,090
Leaving now would be repaying me.

578
00:29:36,290 --> 00:29:39,199
No, Yeong Su said you cannot sleep at all...

579
00:29:39,200 --> 00:29:41,200
and asked me to sleep here with you.

580
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:46,500
He still does not know me at all.

581
00:29:47,810 --> 00:29:49,040
Anyway,

582
00:29:49,110 --> 00:29:52,080
I have prepared everything to help you overcome your insomnia.

583
00:29:56,010 --> 00:29:58,120
But do you have any comfortable clothes I could wear?

584
00:29:59,250 --> 00:30:00,950
Next.

585
00:30:01,020 --> 00:30:04,790
Calcium and magnesium in a 2-to-1 ratio.

586
00:30:07,290 --> 00:30:10,130
And three one-gram pills of melatonin.

587
00:30:11,900 --> 00:30:12,900
Here, take them.

588
00:30:14,900 --> 00:30:18,470
- I take all of these at once? - Oh, of course.

589
00:30:18,570 --> 00:30:20,040
I take them like this every night before bed.

590
00:30:25,180 --> 00:30:27,850
Now, the first one is the cow head pose.

591
00:30:27,910 --> 00:30:30,350
- Like this? - Yes, cross your legs.

592
00:30:30,410 --> 00:30:33,220
Go down just like this, in this way.

593
00:30:33,280 --> 00:30:35,020
Hey, I cannot go down.

594
00:30:35,690 --> 00:30:37,490
No, you have to go down further.

595
00:30:37,520 --> 00:30:38,520
Here.

596
00:30:39,290 --> 00:30:43,590
- Hey, Min! - You have to endure it.

597
00:30:43,660 --> 00:30:46,330
- Stop! - Now, the next one is the cat pose.

598
00:30:47,430 --> 00:30:48,700
Hurry up and try it.

599
00:30:48,770 --> 00:30:51,140
- Stretch more. - Forward...

600
00:30:51,200 --> 00:30:53,270
- You bent your upper body too much. - Oh, well...

601
00:30:53,340 --> 00:30:55,770
- Hey! - That's it. A good stretch, right?

602
00:30:55,840 --> 00:30:58,540
What stretch? Goodness.

603
00:30:58,610 --> 00:31:01,710
Now, the last one is called the happy baby pose.

604
00:31:01,780 --> 00:31:03,410
Lie down.

605
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:07,290
- Oh, this is a bit much, Min. - But this works instantly, really.

606
00:31:07,350 --> 00:31:08,990
- Right here... - Go easy.

607
00:31:09,050 --> 00:31:10,560
- Hey! - Bear with it.

608
00:31:10,620 --> 00:31:14,260
No. Hey!

609
00:31:18,130 --> 00:31:20,700
Now, breathe in through your nose.

610
00:31:23,870 --> 00:31:24,870
Hold it.

611
00:31:26,700 --> 00:31:29,840
And slowly exhale through your mouth.

612
00:31:32,910 --> 00:31:35,080
If you repeat this process four times,

613
00:31:35,150 --> 00:31:36,750
you will soon fall asleep.

614
00:31:39,620 --> 00:31:41,620
Like this is going to make me fall asleep?

615
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:51,230
It does help.

616
00:31:57,470 --> 00:31:58,470
(Writer Kkongkkong's Practice Notebook)

617
00:31:58,540 --> 00:32:00,970
(Writer Kkongkkong, Congratulations on the Grand Prize.)

618
00:32:04,010 --> 00:32:08,780
(Award Ceremony for Recommended Youth Books)

619
00:32:17,150 --> 00:32:18,960
The connection cannot be made. After the beep...

620
00:32:19,020 --> 00:32:20,560
What do we do if the Grand Prize winner does not show?

621
00:32:26,500 --> 00:32:27,970
(Write a post)

622
00:32:32,240 --> 00:32:37,380
(I can't find it!)

623
00:32:53,790 --> 00:32:56,660
We tried to find something as similar to this as possible.

624
00:32:56,730 --> 00:32:58,160
No, look.

625
00:32:58,660 --> 00:33:00,800
The buttons are different, the collar shape is different.

626
00:33:00,870 --> 00:33:03,470
And the most important thing, these stripes.

627
00:33:03,530 --> 00:33:05,670
The thickness of these stripes is different.

628
00:33:07,200 --> 00:33:09,570
Gosh, what do we do now?

629
00:33:10,140 --> 00:33:11,580
Are we supposed to reshoot the connecting scenes too?

630
00:33:12,810 --> 00:33:14,550
I found it!

631
00:33:14,610 --> 00:33:15,610
- What? - Really?

632
00:33:15,680 --> 00:33:17,680
- I found it. - Great job.

633
00:33:17,750 --> 00:33:19,450
I found it.

634
00:33:19,520 --> 00:33:21,550
- I found it. - Good job.

635
00:33:22,990 --> 00:33:26,020
I mean, it definitely was not here just a minute ago.

636
00:33:26,090 --> 00:33:28,030
But after I helped him get dressed and came out,

637
00:33:28,090 --> 00:33:30,390
it was hanging right here as if to show off.

638
00:33:30,460 --> 00:33:32,930
- That is really strange. - Yes.

639
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:36,300
It happens.

640
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:37,400
What?

641
00:33:39,370 --> 00:33:41,240
Did you spray perfume by any chance?

642
00:33:41,270 --> 00:33:42,410
No.

643
00:33:42,440 --> 00:33:45,680
Why would I spray perfume on sponsored clothes? It would stain.

644
00:33:45,740 --> 00:33:46,740
Smell this.

645
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:48,910
What?

646
00:33:49,580 --> 00:33:50,580
What is this?

647
00:33:50,650 --> 00:33:52,280
- You are right. - What?

648
00:33:54,320 --> 00:33:55,750
It smells expensive.

649
00:33:55,820 --> 00:33:57,150
- It is expensive? - Yes.

650
00:33:58,560 --> 00:33:59,560
What is it?

651
00:34:00,660 --> 00:34:02,930
Cut. Okay.

652
00:34:02,990 --> 00:34:06,860
- Great work, everyone. - Great work.

653
00:34:08,470 --> 00:34:11,740
Man, these numbers are not going up at all.

654
00:34:13,240 --> 00:34:15,340
The "Free Egg" score keeps dropping too.

655
00:34:15,970 --> 00:34:20,040
We cannot even make the top five on Lucky Cinema's "Want to See."

656
00:34:20,110 --> 00:34:21,410
We are stuck in sixth place.

657
00:34:22,950 --> 00:34:25,950
We are even ranked lower than movies that have already been released.

658
00:34:29,490 --> 00:34:31,490
What? "Heartsping of Love" rewatch.

659
00:34:31,860 --> 00:34:32,890
This is in fifth place.

660
00:34:33,920 --> 00:34:37,900
You cannot beat Heartsping!

661
00:34:37,960 --> 00:34:39,660
Until the next series comes out,

662
00:34:39,730 --> 00:34:41,330
the kids watch it over and over again.

663
00:34:41,370 --> 00:34:43,630
They watch it at home, and if it is in theaters, they watch it again.

664
00:34:43,700 --> 00:34:45,300
They keep rewatching it just like you do with Moon Bear,

665
00:34:45,370 --> 00:34:46,740
so how can you win?

666
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:49,640
I want to see Moon Bear too.

667
00:34:51,580 --> 00:34:53,210
- Hey. - What?

668
00:34:53,340 --> 00:34:54,710
The premiere is one thing,

669
00:34:54,780 --> 00:34:56,580
but once it is released, everyone will be paying to see it.

670
00:34:56,650 --> 00:34:57,650
Yes.

671
00:34:57,720 --> 00:34:59,350
What if they say it was a waste of money?

672
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:01,350
And when we go around for the stage greetings,

673
00:35:01,420 --> 00:35:02,850
what if only two or three people are sitting there?

674
00:35:02,920 --> 00:35:04,420
Oh, come on, that would never happen.

675
00:35:04,490 --> 00:35:05,490
Just hurry up and go.

676
00:35:06,990 --> 00:35:08,290
I am supposed to be your manager,

677
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:10,630
but I am sorry there is nothing I can do for you.

678
00:35:12,760 --> 00:35:13,960
Wait a minute.

679
00:35:14,030 --> 00:35:16,830
- What? - That smell. It's that perfume.

680
00:35:17,470 --> 00:35:19,300
What perfume smell? Let's go now.

681
00:35:19,370 --> 00:35:21,740
No, it is the same smell from that shirt.

682
00:35:21,810 --> 00:35:24,040
What smell? Come on, let's go.

683
00:35:59,480 --> 00:36:02,250
(I apologize for bothering you.)

684
00:36:05,350 --> 00:36:06,750
Gosh.

685
00:36:06,820 --> 00:36:09,620
Is Tak Mu I making you do things like this now?

686
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:11,220
A sketchbook? How old-fashioned.

687
00:36:12,360 --> 00:36:13,990
Honestly, at this point,

688
00:36:14,060 --> 00:36:16,660
Tak Mu I is the stalker, not me, right?

689
00:36:19,360 --> 00:36:21,929
I thought only job seekers had it hard,

690
00:36:21,930 --> 00:36:24,000
but making a living is tough for managers too.

691
00:36:25,100 --> 00:36:28,070
I mean, if he wants it so badly, he should come himself.

692
00:36:28,170 --> 00:36:30,040
Why make an innocent person suffer?

693
00:36:30,570 --> 00:36:32,480
This is a power trip. What else would you call it?

694
00:36:34,180 --> 00:36:35,350
What?

695
00:36:36,150 --> 00:36:37,750
Oh, my.

696
00:36:37,850 --> 00:36:39,120
Are you crying?

697
00:36:40,420 --> 00:36:42,390
Oh, well, it is about time you let it out.

698
00:36:42,450 --> 00:36:45,460
Here, at least take this off and have a good cry.

699
00:36:45,560 --> 00:36:48,030
Oh, wait, would that be more embarrassing?

700
00:36:48,060 --> 00:36:50,260
Just cry, let it out.

701
00:36:57,870 --> 00:36:59,400
Gosh, the dust...

702
00:37:00,740 --> 00:37:02,140
I have a bit of a dust allergy.

703
00:37:09,050 --> 00:37:10,410
So, why...

704
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:13,480
would someone with allergies wear something like this?

705
00:37:13,550 --> 00:37:14,650
Oh, well...

706
00:37:15,090 --> 00:37:18,060
To show my sincerity about wanting to meet Moon Bear.

707
00:37:18,460 --> 00:37:21,030
- If it is about that... - Oh, no.

708
00:37:21,360 --> 00:37:23,760
I came today to sincerely apologize.

709
00:37:25,460 --> 00:37:27,630
You kept saying you were not, but I treated you like a stalker,

710
00:37:27,700 --> 00:37:29,800
and I am sorry for being rude.

711
00:37:31,240 --> 00:37:33,870
You must have felt offended, and I apologize.

712
00:37:34,710 --> 00:37:36,210
Well, in any case,

713
00:37:36,710 --> 00:37:39,740
you did save me, and with that moth too.

714
00:37:40,540 --> 00:37:43,480
I made you go through things you did not have to,

715
00:37:43,580 --> 00:37:45,580
so I am sorry too.

716
00:37:46,820 --> 00:37:49,350
So, do you accept my apology?

717
00:37:51,160 --> 00:37:52,460
I guess.

718
00:37:53,160 --> 00:37:55,560
But are you okay?

719
00:37:57,530 --> 00:37:58,900
About what?

720
00:37:58,960 --> 00:38:02,800
Oh, last time, you said you really needed that book.

721
00:38:03,900 --> 00:38:05,200
Is something going on?

722
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:10,540
Oh, I do not really want to talk about this, but...

723
00:38:11,780 --> 00:38:13,840
When I was going through a really hard time,

724
00:38:13,910 --> 00:38:15,450
I once went on a trip without a plan.

725
00:38:16,280 --> 00:38:19,020
At that time, my sister said she really wanted me to read it,

726
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:20,249
so she gave me "Byeol I and Moon Bear,"

727
00:38:20,250 --> 00:38:21,420
and that was my first time reading.

728
00:38:23,150 --> 00:38:26,360
Oh, your sister did that.

729
00:38:27,190 --> 00:38:28,460
Anyway,

730
00:38:28,860 --> 00:38:31,160
I found a lot of comfort in reading that book,

731
00:38:33,130 --> 00:38:34,870
and I have been in a similar situation lately.

732
00:38:36,200 --> 00:38:38,070
Maybe it is because I have read it so much.

733
00:38:38,170 --> 00:38:39,770
Volumes 1 and 2 are not enough to fix it.

734
00:38:47,310 --> 00:38:48,310
What?

735
00:38:50,580 --> 00:38:52,050
What? This smell...

736
00:38:52,120 --> 00:38:54,020
What is this smell? Wait...

737
00:38:54,080 --> 00:38:56,290
- What fragrance is that? - What?

738
00:38:58,890 --> 00:39:01,460
Oh, is it my hand cream?

739
00:39:03,960 --> 00:39:07,330
Oh, this is hair perfume.

740
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:10,230
I used it because I did not wash my hair.

741
00:39:10,300 --> 00:39:12,170
But why?

742
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:14,240
No, it is just that it smells exactly like that stalker...

743
00:39:14,300 --> 00:39:15,310
What?

744
00:39:16,370 --> 00:39:17,840
Oh, seriously.

745
00:39:18,110 --> 00:39:19,280
Hey.

746
00:39:20,010 --> 00:39:21,779
I was going to let it go because I felt bad for you.

747
00:39:21,780 --> 00:39:23,850
What? I smell like a stalker?

748
00:39:23,910 --> 00:39:26,149
- Oh, no, that is not what I meant. - Hey.

749
00:39:26,150 --> 00:39:28,220
Is having a handsome face everything?

750
00:39:28,290 --> 00:39:31,160
You are a hopeless narcissist who thinks everyone is into you.

751
00:39:31,220 --> 00:39:32,420
Could you just leave?

752
00:39:32,490 --> 00:39:34,760
Oh, you should really listen to me...

753
00:39:34,830 --> 00:39:36,360
Are you not leaving?

754
00:39:37,390 --> 00:39:38,930
- I will shoot, okay? - No.

755
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:40,200
- Go. - You should really listen to me...

756
00:39:40,260 --> 00:39:42,000
- Go! - No, seriously.

757
00:39:45,770 --> 00:39:46,870
Gosh, seriously.

758
00:39:47,200 --> 00:39:48,240
(I apologize for bothering you.)

759
00:39:49,170 --> 00:39:50,170
Goodness.

760
00:39:55,550 --> 00:39:57,920
(I am sorry for misunderstanding.)

761
00:39:57,980 --> 00:39:59,550
(I am also sorry for being annoying.)

762
00:39:59,620 --> 00:40:03,120
(I was just so curious about what happened to Byeol I and Moon Bear.)

763
00:40:04,490 --> 00:40:06,720
Was I too harsh on a sick person?

764
00:40:10,830 --> 00:40:15,630
(Will you accept my apology?)

765
00:40:17,470 --> 00:40:21,270
Patient Choi Ji Hyeok. Where does it hurt?

766
00:40:21,370 --> 00:40:23,910
Oh, my ears hurt.

767
00:40:24,370 --> 00:40:26,040
Why do your ears hurt?

768
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:28,950
Oh, because of my mom's nagging.

769
00:40:30,050 --> 00:40:31,050
I see.

770
00:40:32,820 --> 00:40:35,690
Well, I will get your medicine ready right away.

771
00:40:35,750 --> 00:40:36,750
Okay.

772
00:40:41,830 --> 00:40:43,460
Here is your medicine.

773
00:40:43,530 --> 00:40:46,130
- Get well soon. - Thank you.

774
00:40:55,270 --> 00:40:56,440
Next patient?

775
00:40:57,440 --> 00:40:58,910
(Poa Kids Cafe, The Kitchen)

776
00:40:58,980 --> 00:41:00,240
(Clockwork Owl Workshop, Hana Neighborhood Park)

777
00:41:08,590 --> 00:41:09,890
May I sit next to you?

778
00:41:29,710 --> 00:41:31,040
You must be a chef.

779
00:41:32,040 --> 00:41:33,080
I am a pharmacist.

780
00:41:34,380 --> 00:41:36,080
Oh, yes.

781
00:41:36,480 --> 00:41:38,120
What kind of food do you make?

782
00:41:40,020 --> 00:41:44,120
Well, I make pasta and steaks.

783
00:41:46,690 --> 00:41:47,890
The kids are so cute, right?

784
00:41:49,760 --> 00:41:52,130
Kids are cute, of course.

785
00:41:53,030 --> 00:41:55,770
The day before yesterday, I asked a kid,

786
00:41:56,100 --> 00:42:00,670
"Where does it hurt?" and he rubbed his chest...

787
00:42:00,740 --> 00:42:03,140
and said, "It hurts here."

788
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:06,140
He said he got rejected after asking a girl in his class out.

789
00:42:11,150 --> 00:42:12,150
That is cute.

790
00:42:13,650 --> 00:42:16,950
Oh, it would be great if there was a medicine for that.

791
00:42:17,890 --> 00:42:19,890
People who failed to get a job,

792
00:42:20,390 --> 00:42:22,430
people who got their hearts broken,

793
00:42:22,490 --> 00:42:24,660
people who are upset because things are not working out.

794
00:42:25,100 --> 00:42:27,970
If those people could just swallow one pill,

795
00:42:28,070 --> 00:42:29,930
their pain would be swallowed up too.

796
00:42:31,400 --> 00:42:33,340
If I could make a medicine like that,

797
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:35,240
I would study really hard...

798
00:42:35,310 --> 00:42:37,640
and it would be nice to become a pharmacist.

799
00:42:37,710 --> 00:42:39,910
I have thoughts like that.

800
00:42:41,140 --> 00:42:42,150
Goodness.

801
00:42:49,420 --> 00:42:50,890
Oh, I am sorry.

802
00:42:50,950 --> 00:42:53,820
I talked too much to someone I just met, right?

803
00:42:53,920 --> 00:42:56,430
No, it is not because of that.

804
00:42:59,100 --> 00:43:01,370
That is mine.

805
00:43:02,800 --> 00:43:05,300
Excuse me? Oh, my goodness.

806
00:43:05,740 --> 00:43:08,440
Oh, my, I am sorry. What should I do about this?

807
00:43:08,510 --> 00:43:10,470
I already put my mouth on it.

808
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:18,520
You put your room up for rent?

809
00:43:19,750 --> 00:43:21,690
Do you know what the best part about this place is?

810
00:43:22,820 --> 00:43:24,820
Well, the best part?

811
00:43:26,660 --> 00:43:27,990
The view?

812
00:43:28,230 --> 00:43:31,760
- The sunset? - No, the address.

813
00:43:32,460 --> 00:43:33,960
The address?

814
00:43:34,060 --> 00:43:35,700
When I lived in a semi-basement,

815
00:43:35,770 --> 00:43:39,000
I hated that I always had to write "basement" in front of it.

816
00:43:39,040 --> 00:43:40,640
But if I did not write it,

817
00:43:40,740 --> 00:43:43,140
all my packages and mail would go to the first floor.

818
00:43:44,780 --> 00:43:48,110
But here, you cannot tell just by looking at the address.

819
00:43:49,880 --> 00:43:51,210
Cut, okay.

820
00:43:51,650 --> 00:43:53,380
- Let us take a short break. - Yes.

821
00:43:53,450 --> 00:43:54,890
We are taking a break.

822
00:44:02,430 --> 00:44:04,630
Darn. It's Mu I again.

823
00:44:05,730 --> 00:44:06,900
Hi, there.

824
00:44:08,500 --> 00:44:10,470
Oh, hi.

825
00:44:10,600 --> 00:44:13,270
Producer Yeon Ju said you are a job seeker.

826
00:44:13,840 --> 00:44:15,770
You know I am playing a job seeker in this drama too, right?

827
00:44:16,840 --> 00:44:18,910
Oh, yes, I heard.

828
00:44:18,980 --> 00:44:21,850
I am having a hard time getting a feel for it.

829
00:44:21,910 --> 00:44:25,150
Should I call it an interview? Or research?

830
00:44:25,780 --> 00:44:28,750
Oh, right, consulting. Could I ask you for some advice?

831
00:44:36,730 --> 00:44:38,660
Are you not scared living in a place like this?

832
00:44:41,060 --> 00:44:42,500
I am scared.

833
00:44:42,570 --> 00:44:45,240
That is why I keep my doors locked and double-locked.

834
00:44:49,240 --> 00:44:51,170
Oh, what is it like living as a job seeker?

835
00:44:53,110 --> 00:44:54,950
Well, let me see.

836
00:44:56,250 --> 00:44:57,480
How should I put it?

837
00:44:59,380 --> 00:45:01,080
It feels like I am floating.

838
00:45:04,190 --> 00:45:06,060
Oh, just like that,

839
00:45:07,420 --> 00:45:11,760
I am definitely growing, and I am living well day by day,

840
00:45:12,130 --> 00:45:14,630
but it feels like I cannot put my roots down in the ground.

841
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:17,230
Are you not anxious?

842
00:45:19,540 --> 00:45:20,540
No.

843
00:45:21,670 --> 00:45:23,770
Even on nights when nothing happens,

844
00:45:24,910 --> 00:45:26,410
the towels dry,

845
00:45:26,840 --> 00:45:28,210
the plants grow,

846
00:45:28,280 --> 00:45:30,610
and packages just arrive in front of the house.

847
00:45:31,180 --> 00:45:34,220
I believe something is happening during my nights too.

848
00:45:34,790 --> 00:45:36,150
I do not doubt it.

849
00:45:36,220 --> 00:45:39,020
If I do not believe in myself, who will?

850
00:45:39,090 --> 00:45:42,990
Oh, that is so cool, Yu Il. I can call you Yu Il, right?

851
00:45:43,660 --> 00:45:45,130
Yes.

852
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:46,200
You are cool.

853
00:45:52,470 --> 00:45:53,470
Hold on a second.

854
00:46:01,880 --> 00:46:03,080
What are you doing here?

855
00:46:04,210 --> 00:46:06,420
Oh, I was just wondering what all this was.

856
00:46:07,880 --> 00:46:10,590
What do you mean? They are cacti.

857
00:46:11,090 --> 00:46:12,420
Do you seriously not know what a cactus is?

858
00:46:14,360 --> 00:46:17,290
Oh, so these are all cacti. I see.

859
00:46:18,930 --> 00:46:21,600
Da Hong, when you live alone,

860
00:46:22,100 --> 00:46:24,470
you have to be especially careful of people like him.

861
00:46:24,940 --> 00:46:27,400
Mu I, were you eavesdropping?

862
00:46:27,440 --> 00:46:29,140
Were you curious about what I was doing?

863
00:46:29,210 --> 00:46:33,480
- No, it is not like that... - Come on, I know it is.

864
00:46:33,540 --> 00:46:36,250
You were so curious because I was out of sight.

865
00:46:36,680 --> 00:46:37,950
Seriously!

866
00:46:40,320 --> 00:46:42,620
So they have that kind of relationship.

867
00:46:46,060 --> 00:46:49,130
By the way, Yu Il, you must really like Ryu Min.

868
00:46:49,590 --> 00:46:51,030
Oh, right.

869
00:46:51,090 --> 00:46:52,800
Thank you for the tea.

870
00:46:52,900 --> 00:46:54,259
- Da Hong, get ready. - Okay.

871
00:46:54,260 --> 00:46:55,630
Thank you, Yu Il. See you later.

872
00:46:57,630 --> 00:46:59,870
- Hello. - Hello.

873
00:47:00,270 --> 00:47:02,510
You must be a fan of Ryu Min.

874
00:47:03,570 --> 00:47:05,880
Gosh, that is impressive for a job seeker.

875
00:47:06,740 --> 00:47:08,040
Do your parents not mind?

876
00:47:08,550 --> 00:47:10,450
Oh, parents usually do not like this kind of thing.

877
00:47:10,650 --> 00:47:11,680
- Director. - Yes.

878
00:47:11,750 --> 00:47:14,280
- I brought this for you to drink. - Oh, my, how thoughtful.

879
00:47:14,890 --> 00:47:17,220
Your shoulders are really tense, Director.

880
00:47:17,290 --> 00:47:19,560
- Let me massage them for you. - What? Okay.

881
00:47:20,820 --> 00:47:21,960
That feels good.

882
00:47:22,560 --> 00:47:24,790
- They are so tense. - Gosh.

883
00:47:24,860 --> 00:47:26,060
Stop it.

884
00:47:26,260 --> 00:47:27,760
- Gosh! - It feels refreshing, right?

885
00:47:28,170 --> 00:47:31,700
Gosh, stop. I said, stop!

886
00:47:33,370 --> 00:47:35,140
I told you to stop!

887
00:47:35,210 --> 00:47:37,640
Hurry up and get ready. Gosh, it hurts.

888
00:47:37,940 --> 00:47:39,540
Well, they were just really tense.

889
00:47:43,710 --> 00:47:46,920
That was partly to apologize for eavesdropping earlier...

890
00:47:46,980 --> 00:47:47,980
and partly revenge on your behalf.

891
00:47:49,920 --> 00:47:52,060
I never asked you to get revenge for me.

892
00:47:52,120 --> 00:47:54,990
No matter what you do, I cannot give you the book.

893
00:47:57,030 --> 00:47:58,230
Then sell it to me.

894
00:48:00,430 --> 00:48:01,830
How much will you give me?

895
00:48:02,300 --> 00:48:04,300
Oh, you would know if you had eavesdropped earlier.

896
00:48:04,400 --> 00:48:06,840
I am a job seeker, so I am struggling a lot.

897
00:48:07,400 --> 00:48:09,510
About 100,000 dollars?

898
00:48:09,570 --> 00:48:10,710
I will sell it if you give me that.

899
00:48:13,210 --> 00:48:14,340
You are a total thief.

900
00:48:17,750 --> 00:48:20,280
Gosh. First a stalker, and now...

901
00:48:20,780 --> 00:48:21,850
a thief?

902
00:48:23,850 --> 00:48:26,520
Will you get out before I report you for trespassing?

903
00:48:27,560 --> 00:48:28,890
That is not what I meant.

904
00:48:28,960 --> 00:48:30,230
Get out!

905
00:48:33,500 --> 00:48:34,500
Seriously.

906
00:48:34,560 --> 00:48:35,930
(Flowers bloom on the rooftop too.)

907
00:48:46,340 --> 00:48:50,410
Are you getting even skinnier? Please get some sleep today.

908
00:48:50,480 --> 00:48:52,150
You are going to end up in serious trouble at this rate.

909
00:48:53,920 --> 00:48:57,390
Moon Bear, where are you?

910
00:48:57,450 --> 00:49:00,320
If you can hear me, please answer.

911
00:49:03,030 --> 00:49:05,800
I think you need help from a medical professional.

912
00:49:05,860 --> 00:49:07,730
I wonder if Jae Gyu is still at the hospital.

913
00:49:07,800 --> 00:49:11,000
Forget it. Jae Gyu is completely unsympathetic.

914
00:49:11,070 --> 00:49:12,940
He will prescribe sleeping pills instead of empathizing.

915
00:49:18,640 --> 00:49:19,640
What is this?

916
00:49:21,340 --> 00:49:22,910
What is that now?

917
00:49:22,980 --> 00:49:24,980
A YouTube reunion frequency.

918
00:49:25,050 --> 00:49:26,720
Min said it was good.

919
00:49:26,780 --> 00:49:29,590
It is the desire of our generation...

920
00:49:29,650 --> 00:49:31,350
to somehow reconnect with our exes, I guess?

921
00:49:33,560 --> 00:49:35,330
If I keep listening to it,

922
00:49:35,390 --> 00:49:38,500
my broken connection with Moon Bear might be restored.

923
00:49:38,560 --> 00:49:40,230
Unbelievable.

924
00:49:40,300 --> 00:49:45,200
Okay, if you are into shamanism, let's just go there instead.

925
00:49:47,500 --> 00:49:48,510
Go where?

926
00:49:53,140 --> 00:49:55,050
Why do you have this stuff in your house?

927
00:49:55,110 --> 00:49:56,780
Is it not distracting?

928
00:49:57,080 --> 00:49:58,920
What are you curious about?

929
00:50:00,220 --> 00:50:02,690
So what does she do again?

930
00:50:02,750 --> 00:50:06,460
Not "she." I am Tarot Master Rosa.

931
00:50:07,160 --> 00:50:08,590
Master?

932
00:50:08,660 --> 00:50:09,990
You cannot even play Go-Stop.

933
00:50:10,060 --> 00:50:12,930
Darn it. I am not doing this. Take him away.

934
00:50:13,000 --> 00:50:14,500
All right.

935
00:50:14,560 --> 00:50:15,800
You, Da Hong...

936
00:50:17,500 --> 00:50:21,040
- Rosa. - You saw Rosa catch Min Ye, right?

937
00:50:21,100 --> 00:50:23,370
She is really good at this. She is spot on.

938
00:50:23,440 --> 00:50:26,180
What does that have to do with this?

939
00:50:27,610 --> 00:50:28,610
Rosa?

940
00:50:32,720 --> 00:50:36,090
Think about what you want to know, and pick a card.

941
00:50:43,560 --> 00:50:45,960
The Devil card represents strong desire,

942
00:50:46,030 --> 00:50:48,300
obsession, and lingering attachment.

943
00:50:49,000 --> 00:50:51,530
You must want something very badly.

944
00:50:52,070 --> 00:50:56,070
To the other person, you might seem like a devil.

945
00:51:00,980 --> 00:51:01,980
Well...

946
00:51:03,280 --> 00:51:05,520
Will I be able to find what I'm looking for?

947
00:51:05,580 --> 00:51:06,750
Pick one more card.

948
00:51:18,630 --> 00:51:19,900
Death.

949
00:51:19,960 --> 00:51:22,200
That's right, the writer is dead, right?

950
00:51:22,270 --> 00:51:26,070
- Or does he die? - No.

951
00:51:26,470 --> 00:51:29,210
The world of tarot is not that simple.

952
00:51:29,270 --> 00:51:33,410
An ending can also mean a new beginning.

953
00:51:35,310 --> 00:51:37,550
So, will I find it or not?

954
00:51:38,950 --> 00:51:43,690
The current phase will end, and you will face a new phase.

955
00:51:46,060 --> 00:51:47,860
It means you'll find it.

956
00:51:47,920 --> 00:51:49,230
Where is it? Where do I need to go?

957
00:52:04,510 --> 00:52:06,880
What does this card mean?

958
00:52:09,980 --> 00:52:11,450
Well, that is...

959
00:52:11,510 --> 00:52:13,920
What is this handwriting?

960
00:52:15,450 --> 00:52:16,450
Right.

961
00:52:17,650 --> 00:52:20,990
Does it mean "unique" in Italian?

962
00:52:21,320 --> 00:52:23,930
It meant something like that.

963
00:52:26,560 --> 00:52:27,800
What?

964
00:52:27,860 --> 00:52:30,130
What? Only one?

965
00:52:44,680 --> 00:52:45,680
Yes.

966
00:52:47,950 --> 00:52:50,690
I found it. It was on the desk.

967
00:52:51,120 --> 00:52:55,360
Oh, what a relief. Could you bring it to the set?

968
00:52:55,430 --> 00:52:57,960
It has the schedule and everything.

969
00:52:58,030 --> 00:53:01,300
- I'm sorry, Yu Il. - Oh, don't be sorry.

970
00:53:01,360 --> 00:53:02,370
Where should I go?

971
00:53:03,370 --> 00:53:05,030
("Rooftop Romance")

972
00:53:05,100 --> 00:53:06,870
(Way to go, Tak Mu I!)

973
00:53:06,940 --> 00:53:09,740
(Supporting Actor Tak Mu I and the "Rooftop Romance" team)

974
00:53:13,340 --> 00:53:15,080
- Thanks for the drink. - Enjoy.

975
00:53:15,140 --> 00:53:16,480
Enjoy.

976
00:53:16,610 --> 00:53:17,950
You regret doing a romance with Da Hong, right?

977
00:53:19,780 --> 00:53:21,120
I'll have a latte, please.

978
00:53:21,450 --> 00:53:25,860
Why? I like it. I get to hug and kiss him.

979
00:53:25,920 --> 00:53:28,630
I'm begging the writer because there's no deep kiss scene.

980
00:53:28,690 --> 00:53:31,130
Hey, there are a lot of people here.

981
00:53:31,190 --> 00:53:33,560
If you do not want to be on camera, just do it now.

982
00:53:34,760 --> 00:53:36,400
What do you want to drink?

983
00:53:36,470 --> 00:53:37,470
I'll have...

984
00:53:38,700 --> 00:53:42,870
- Hey. - Thanks, Yu Il. You saved my life.

985
00:53:42,940 --> 00:53:45,610
Here. Are you on a break right now?

986
00:53:45,710 --> 00:53:48,340
Yes, as you can see, a coffee truck arrived.

987
00:53:48,410 --> 00:53:49,410
Wait just a minute.

988
00:53:49,480 --> 00:53:50,779
I will get some stuff done...

989
00:53:50,780 --> 00:53:52,320
- and get us coffee. - Okay.

990
00:53:56,590 --> 00:53:57,720
What?

991
00:53:58,320 --> 00:53:59,890
The Tower. Only one.

992
00:54:01,020 --> 00:54:02,490
What are you talking about?

993
00:54:02,560 --> 00:54:04,390
She's the only way.

994
00:54:05,500 --> 00:54:07,360
(Supporting Actor Tak Mu I and the "Rooftop Romance" team)

995
00:54:09,230 --> 00:54:10,570
Who is that?

996
00:54:10,630 --> 00:54:13,000
Oh, she's the one who lives in the rooftop apartment...

997
00:54:13,070 --> 00:54:14,470
I live in on the show.

998
00:54:14,540 --> 00:54:15,670
She's a friend of the junior producer.

999
00:54:18,370 --> 00:54:19,540
What brings you here?

1000
00:54:21,210 --> 00:54:23,110
Oh, I had some business to take care of.

1001
00:54:23,180 --> 00:54:26,320
Of course, that business does not involve you.

1002
00:54:26,480 --> 00:54:29,350
And could you please pretend not to know me if you see me?

1003
00:54:29,420 --> 00:54:31,050
You should stay away from your stalker.

1004
00:54:31,120 --> 00:54:33,590
If you keep being nice to me, I might get the wrong idea.

1005
00:54:36,990 --> 00:54:38,760
Have this. It is new.

1006
00:54:39,530 --> 00:54:41,900
Oh, I am fine. My friend is bringing me one.

1007
00:54:45,000 --> 00:54:46,000
Hey,

1008
00:54:46,070 --> 00:54:47,600
- Yes? - Thank you for the coffee.

1009
00:54:47,670 --> 00:54:48,670
Sure.

1010
00:54:49,510 --> 00:54:51,070
Oh, hello, Lim Su Kyung.

1011
00:54:52,980 --> 00:54:53,980
Oh, hi.

1012
00:54:55,810 --> 00:54:57,180
Lim Su Kyung?

1013
00:54:58,880 --> 00:55:00,620
This is Gong Yu Il.

1014
00:55:00,880 --> 00:55:02,820
Oh, I am sorry.

1015
00:55:04,190 --> 00:55:05,220
Oh, it is fine.

1016
00:55:06,560 --> 00:55:07,690
Darn it.

1017
00:55:07,760 --> 00:55:10,460
After leaving my room in that state,

1018
00:55:10,530 --> 00:55:12,330
I cannot exactly say I am not your fan now.

1019
00:55:13,860 --> 00:55:17,030
Would you like to have this? I just got it.

1020
00:55:17,130 --> 00:55:19,940
Oh, yes, thank you.

1021
00:55:20,400 --> 00:55:23,170
It will probably taste even better since you gave it to me.

1022
00:55:24,670 --> 00:55:27,580
Did you get the limited edition photocard this time?

1023
00:55:28,610 --> 00:55:30,250
Oh, the photocard?

1024
00:55:31,480 --> 00:55:32,480
Not yet.

1025
00:55:33,920 --> 00:55:35,550
Then I will bring it to you.

1026
00:55:36,090 --> 00:55:37,090
Just a moment.

1027
00:55:40,760 --> 00:55:44,290
But why would celebrity merchandise include poker cards?

1028
00:55:44,360 --> 00:55:45,960
It is not like they are encouraging gambling.

1029
00:55:47,500 --> 00:55:48,970
You do not know what a photocard is?

1030
00:55:50,070 --> 00:55:51,070
Photocard.

1031
00:55:53,700 --> 00:55:55,070
Oh, photocard!

1032
00:55:56,370 --> 00:55:57,370
Right.

1033
00:55:58,810 --> 00:56:01,280
A superfan who does not even know what a photocard is.

1034
00:56:01,340 --> 00:56:03,680
And you flat-out rejected what I offered,

1035
00:56:03,750 --> 00:56:05,620
but you accepted Min's right away.

1036
00:56:05,680 --> 00:56:07,650
It is clear you are not my fan.

1037
00:56:08,180 --> 00:56:10,090
You sure figured that out quickly.

1038
00:56:10,150 --> 00:56:12,660
If you have nothing else to say, you can leave now.

1039
00:56:13,120 --> 00:56:15,830
No, I have a ton of things to say.

1040
00:56:30,340 --> 00:56:31,840
(Way to go, Tak Mu I!)

1041
00:56:54,000 --> 00:56:55,160
("To You")

1042
00:56:55,230 --> 00:56:58,270
(Epilogue)

1043
00:57:11,450 --> 00:57:13,820
Mu I, take this with you.

1044
00:57:14,420 --> 00:57:15,950
I think it is a book you really need.

1045
00:57:17,250 --> 00:57:18,250
Really?

1046
00:57:23,530 --> 00:57:26,360
("Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 2, "Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 3)
